atural Colours Transition in Confectionery"},{"description":"Increased US regulatory dialogue and RFK Jr.'s MAHA initiative push food companies like Mars to offer dye-free options in M&Ms by 2026, though full transition awaits scalable solutions.[2]","title":"Regulatory Pressure on Synthetic Dyes"},{"description":"Mars-Disney Marvel collab for M&Ms in 2026 highlights trend of cross-fandom partnerships delivering immersive experiences, limited products to drive engagement across 65 markets.[3]","title":"Global Brand Collaborations Boost"},{"description":"Appointment of CCO for Mars Food & Nutrition signals focus on commercial excellence and retail partnerships to accelerate portfolio growth including M&Ms in North America.[6]","title":"Sales Leadership for Growth"}],"industryType":"Tech","joiningAvailability":null,"languages":{"English":""},"linkedinUrl":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/mahavir-sancheti/","location":"Pune, Maharashtra, India","name":"Mahavir Sancheti","notes":[],"objections":[{"cialdini":"Social Proof","counter":"I hear that—others in manufacturing felt the same until they saw how GrokHR cut their time-to-hire by 50% during compliance rushes, with seamless India tax integrations their old vendor lacked. What specific gaps are you seeing right now?","number":1,"objection":"We already have an HR system in place.","whyWorks":["Feel-Felt-Found disarms resistance (Sandler)","Reframe with Challenger insight on niche fit (JOLT)"]},{"cialdini":"Consistency","counter":"Totally get the squeeze from the dye transitions—our manufacturing clients found GrokHR paid for itself in 3 months by slashing admin costs 30-40% and avoiding compliance fines. Curious, what's your biggest cost leak in HR right now?","number":2,"objection":"Budget is tight with these product launches.","whyWorks":["Negative reverse uncovers real budget drivers","Quantified ROI overcomes indecision (JOLT)"]}],"phone":null,"photo":null,"postImpressionsLast7Days":null,"preferredRoles":[],"productFit"